{
  "dom_id": "step-q46580",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=4,{t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $P(t).$",
  "worked_solution": "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=4$ and ${t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(2)(t-4)(t-3) \\\\  & =2(t-4)(t-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-4)(t-3) & =2({t}^{2}-7t+12) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-14t+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=2{t}^{2}-14t+24.$",
